    """Convert a histogram to a graph.

    Args:
        hist: A histogram object.
        make_value: A function to set the value of a graph's point. By default,
            it is the bin content.
        get_coordinate: Defines what the coordinate of a graph point created from
            a histogram bin will be. It can be "left" (default), "right", or
            "middle".
        field_names: Field names of the graph. Their number must be the same as
            the dimension of the result. For a make_value above, they would be
            ("x", "y_mean", "y_mean_error").
